Spec: Lesson entity

Purpose:
  The Lesson entity: a date, a start time and an end time, a topic, free-text notes and a reference to a
  CourseRealization. A view-less, route-less package used by ../realizations/realizations.sdd,
  ../semester/semester.sdd and ../day_dialog/day_dialog.sdd.

Owns:
  ./domain.py
  ./ports.py
  ./services.py
  ./repository_sqlite.py

References:
  ../architecture.sdd

Depends on:
  ../shared/shared.sdd
  ../realizations/realizations.sdd
  ../no_teach_weeks/no_teach_weeks.sdd

Must:
  A Lesson has a date, a start time and an end time, a topic, free-text notes and a reference to a CourseRealization.
  At most one Lesson exists for a date and CourseRealization; a second Lesson on that date is rejected with
    @InvalidLessonError.
  A single Lesson is edited and removed from ../realizations/realizations.sdd's weekly table, which owns those
    affordances and their routes; this package stays view-less and route-less.
  @LessonService.add_lesson validates that the CourseRealization id exists (through
    ../realizations/realizations.sdd's ports.py, per ../architecture.sdd), that the topic is non-empty and that the
    end time is later than the start time, rejecting with @UnknownRealizationError or @InvalidLessonError before
    storage.
  @LessonService.add_lesson also rejects a date inside a NoTeachWeek of the CourseRealization's Semester, read through
    ../no_teach_weeks/no_teach_weeks.sdd, with @InvalidLessonError, because nothing is taught during such a week.
  @LessonService.update_lesson applies the same checks as @LessonService.add_lesson, ignoring the Lesson being
    edited when looking for the date it already occupies, and keeps the CourseRealization the Lesson already
    belongs to; it rejects an unknown id with @UnknownLessonError.
  @LessonService.delete_lesson removes one Lesson and leaves its CourseRealization and the realization's other
    Lessons untouched, rejecting an unknown id with @UnknownLessonError.
  @LessonRepository in ./ports.py exposes operations to get, list lessons for a CourseRealization or a date range,
    to add, update and delete one Lesson and to delete every lesson of a CourseRealization.
  @LessonService.delete_lessons_for_realization removes all of a CourseRealization's Lessons, which
    ../realizations/realizations.sdd's @RealizationService calls before removing that realization so no Lesson is
    left pointing at it.
  Lesson listings are ordered by date and start time, so a day with several Lessons reads chronologically.
  The table is created automatically on startup when it does not exist.

Tasks:
  [x] Implement @Lesson in ./domain.py and a hardcoded ./services.py returning placeholder Lessons for each
    placeholder CourseRealization across the hardcoded Semester, standing in for @LessonRepository until
    persistence exists
  [x] Replace the hardcoded ./services.py with a class-based @LessonRepository-backed `LessonService`
    (./ports.py and ./repository_sqlite.py), per ../architecture.sdd's Example
  [x] Validate the CourseRealization id (via ../realizations/realizations.sdd's ports.py), a non-empty topic and
    start-before-end times in @LessonService.add_lesson with @UnknownRealizationError and @InvalidLessonError
  [x] Reject a lesson dated inside a NoTeachWeek of the CourseRealization's Semester with @InvalidLessonError
  [x] Add @LessonService.delete_lessons_for_realization, which ../realizations/realizations.sdd's
    @RealizationService.delete_realization calls when it removes a realization
  [x] Decide that a single Lesson may be edited and deleted from the UI, and that at most one Lesson exists per
    date and CourseRealization
  [x] Add @LessonService.get_lesson, @LessonService.update_lesson and @LessonService.delete_lesson with the
    matching @LessonRepository operations, and reject a date already holding a Lesson with @InvalidLessonError
